WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.033
-First, we're about to
face off in a game of Drinko.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:05.434
Drinko, do you want to explain
how the game works?

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:08.834
-Yes. Welcome to Drinko.
In this game, the two of you

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.334
will take turns
climbing my stairs

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.567
and dropping two of your disks
down the Drinko board.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:16.167
The disks will plink down
and land in these plastic cups

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:18.767
containing some of my favorite
beverages such as...

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.501
Girl Scout Thin Mints,

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.968
cream-cheese water,
and garlic shot.

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:26.133
Your opponent
must drink the cocktail

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.901
of the two chosen drinks.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:30.267
-Alright. Thank you very much.
-Cheese water?

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.734
-Drinko, what did you say again?
Did you say --

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.200
-Cream-cheese water!
-Alright.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.434
-♪ It's water
with cream cheese! ♪

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.234
-That's my favorite --

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.100
That's a great
Harry styles song.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.100
♪ Cream-cheese water, ah,
cream-cheese water ♪

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.934
Alright, Miles,
why don't you go up there first

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.701
because you're our guest?
-Sure.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:49.267
-Climb up the steps of Drinko
and enjoy yourself

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:50.801
a good beverage.
-Yes. Thank you.

00:00:50.801 --> 00:00:52.000
-Yeah, no problem.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:54.901
-Drinko, you okay?

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.834
-Drop the disk whenever
you're ready, Miles.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:01:01.033
-Alright.
-Here it comes.

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.968
Cream-cheese water!

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.100
-Alright. Your first cup
will be the garlic shot.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.567
-Garlic shot!
-[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.567
-It's a garlic shot.
-That's healthy.

00:01:10.567 --> 00:01:12.400
-That's healthy for you.
That's not that bad.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.501
And then you're gonna mix that
with another beverage

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.133
once you drop the second chip.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.734
-Drop your second disks.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.868
Here it comes.

00:01:20.868 --> 00:01:24.000
Coming down the stairway.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.934
Ginger kombucha.
-Ooh. Not bad actually.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.734
-Ginger kombucha.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:30.434
-Oh, my -- I'm -- This is great.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.267
-Miles, you have
ginger kombucha...

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.767
Thank you, Drinko.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.234
-I think they sell these --
-You wanna take those?

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.734
-You can buy this shot in a
store right now for like $14.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.067
-Yeah, that's actually not bad.

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.501
You've got ginger kombucha
and garlic shot.

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.067
Not bad.
-Ooh.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:47.534
-Place it in this nice cup
right there and enjoy yourself.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:49.934
A garlic shot.

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.968
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:54.801
-Mmm!
-Alright.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.567
♪♪

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.234
Good luck. Good to see you.

00:01:59.234 --> 00:02:00.767
-Oh!

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.701
-Oh, that'll help.
That'll help.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.601
-God, it's --

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.434
♪♪

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:13.934
-Ahh. I feel lighter.
I don't know. I feel --

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.868
I'm so much healthier
than you right now.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:18.434
-Your Adam's apple was shaking
as you were drinking.

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.734
[ Gurgling ]

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:23.901
-Yeah.
-Now it is your turn, James.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.934
-What do you want me to do,
Drinko?

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.467
-I want you
to ascend the staircase

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.901
and drop two disks in me.
-Okay.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:32.901
-Drinko's getting
a little bossy.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:35.067
-Drinko.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.334
-I'm sorry. On me. All over me.

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:38.934
-Alright, all right.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.567
-Climb the -- Unh! Eh! Ah!

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:47.000
Unh! Eee! Ooh! Ooh! Ohh...

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.934
Drop the disk, baby.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.100
♪♪

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.300
-Alright. I want to stay away
from cream-cheese water.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.200
-No.
-I'm going to throw up

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.000
if I do cream-cheese water.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.067
Is that good right here?

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.634
-Here we go.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:04.234
-No! Stay away from that side!
Yes! Good, good, good.

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:06.033
Oh, no, oh, no!

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.133
-No! Yoo-hoo!

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:10.734
-Yoo-hoo! Yes!

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.100
-Drop the second disk.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.000
-Ugh. Let's just do it.
Alright. Here we go.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.100
-Come on, cream-cheese water!

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.534
[ Drinko grunting ]

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.033
-No, no, no. Please.
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:25.167
-Hey!

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:34.067
♪♪

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.467
Oh, James.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:40.334
You must drink
my cream-cheese water.

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:43.734
-I hate this game. I --

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.701
I just -- It's not.
-That's the cream --

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:47.400
-It is not!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.167
♪♪

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.033
Why in the world?!

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:56.100
-♪ Cream-cheese water ♪

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.334
Two drinks, one cup.

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.501
[ Audience groans ]
There you go.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.334
♪♪

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.367
-Ugh!
-Cream-cheese water.

00:04:04.367 --> 00:04:06.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:09.000
-I mean, it might pair well
with Yoo-hoo.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.033
-You can do it, James.
You can do it.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.767
Oh, that's the Yoo-hoo.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:18.968
♪♪

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:22.567
-[ Groans ] I really --
This type of stuff. I can't --

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.133
I can't do it. I can't.
Like --

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.100
-You can do it. You can do it.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:30.567
-[ Coughs ]

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:33.234
♪♪

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.167
[ Coughs ]

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:38.834
♪♪

00:04:38.834 --> 00:04:40.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:43.334
♪♪

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:45.067
-Wow!

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:48.734
♪♪

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.400
Ohh!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.234
-How's that?
-Not so bad.

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:54.100
-It's so gross.
-Yeah.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.501
-It's so --
What's the worst part is,

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:57.467
it's still in the beard.

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.834
[ Laughter ]
It is so gross.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.934
Gosh, that is disgusting.
Okay.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.167
-Cream-cheese water.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:05.067
Are you ready
for the final round?

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:08.234
-Yeah. Okay.
This is gonna be a race.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:11.067
We're both gonna climb up
there. It's not over now?

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:13.901
-No, one more round.
-What's the final round?

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:16.133
-Both of you climb up
and drop a disk.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.534
Whosever first disk lands first
is the winner,

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:22.501
and the loser has to drink
the cocktail of both beverages.

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:24.334
♪ Let's go ♪

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.501
♪♪

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:28.067
-Oh. Wait. What is it?

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.334
-Both of you
climb up the stairs.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.734
-Alright.
-Both of you drop a disk.

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:35.434
-We're dropping two disks?
-Yes, at the same time.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.601
Whoever's disk gets there
first wins.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:43.467
The other person has to drink
the drink, the loser's drink.

00:05:43.467 --> 00:05:46.567
-I think the Drinko guy
is drunk. I don't think --

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.501
-Oh, yeah.
-That's why they call me Drinko.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:50.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.734
-Drinko, wait.
Where do we find you, Drinko?

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:55.968
-Ready?
I'm going to count to three.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.000
-Drinko, where did we find you?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.634
-You didn't find me.
I found you.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:04.033
-Alright.
So we're both dropping --

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.834
We're both dropping
at the same time.

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:08.133
-At the same time. I will
count down, "3, 2, 1, drop."

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.267
Are you ready?
-Yes.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:10.868
Where are you putting yours?
On the line?

00:06:10.868 --> 00:06:12.601
-Right here.
-Okay.

00:06:12.601 --> 00:06:16.200
-3, 2, 1, drop.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:19.000
♪♪

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.033
-Oh, I'm toast.
-Yo!

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.133
-What'd you get?

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:25.567
What did we get?
What did we get?

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.834
Is it more cream-cheese water!

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:29.634
This is the best game ever!

00:06:29.634 --> 00:06:32.534
Drinko, Drinko, Drinko!
Drinko, Drinko, Drinko!

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.934
What did we get?
Yoo-hoo...

00:06:34.934 --> 00:06:36.567
-Well, I think I've got the...

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:38.133
-And the garlic shot again?
Dude.

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:40.634
-Oh, garlic shot.
-What do you -- What do you --

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.667
I'll give you -- You can add
one more thing to mine.

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:44.667
-Okay.
-Bone broth.

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:46.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.501 --> 00:06:49.501
[ Audience
shouting suggestions ]

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.334
-Mustard juice.

00:06:51.334 --> 00:06:55.234
♪♪

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:58.000
Cream-cheese water.
-No.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.534 --> 00:07:03.767
They -- The audience
turned on me so fast.

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:05.100
It's like...

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.701
-They loved you
when you come out.

00:07:06.701 --> 00:07:08.234
-I come out. They're like,
"Oh, 'Top Gun," this and that."

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:10.200
For this, they're like...
-"Cream-cheese water."

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.567
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You guys are mean.

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:14.601
-Good luck. Are you -- Do you
have a good, strong stomach?

00:07:14.601 --> 00:07:18.901
-No. I do have, like, a fairly
sensitive gag reflex.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:21.467
-I can't think about what I did.
The Yoo-hoo helped me.

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:24.100
The Yoo-hoo helped me.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:27.300
That's not Yoo-hoo.
That's garlic.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.534
And that's the Yoo-hoo.
-Here comes the Yoo-hoo.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:34.367
-I'm gonna add a little
cranberry into this one.

00:07:34.367 --> 00:07:36.567
-Oh, my God.
-Take it to the "finish."

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:39.300
-That's a lot to chug.
-Turn and burn, baby.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:44.601
-Oh, my God! Legend!

00:07:44.601 --> 00:07:46.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:46.968 --> 00:07:50.868
♪♪

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:52.033
Legend right there!

00:07:52.033 --> 00:07:55.100
-i haven't seen you
since "Top Gun: Maverick"

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.334
was the number-one --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:57.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:07:57.601 --> 00:07:58.901
-The number-one movie that --
I think it's --

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.133
I think it's --
I think it's the fifth highest

00:08:01.133 --> 00:08:02.701
grossing film
in American history.

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:03.834
-Yeah.
-Congratulations, buddy.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.234
-Yeah, still climbing.
-You did it.

00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:07.567
-Every day.
-Yeah, every -- that is correct.

00:08:07.567 --> 00:08:10.067
-Yeah.
-Uh, it's bigger than

00:08:10.067 --> 00:08:11.234
we even thought
it was gonna be.

00:08:11.234 --> 00:08:13.133
-Oh, for sure.
-It was fantastic.

00:08:13.133 --> 00:08:15.234
-I know, people just --
people really love --

00:08:15.234 --> 00:08:17.434
Well, they love Tom Cruise,
which -- as they should.

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:18.734
He's dedicated...
-Of course.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.434
-...so much of his life
to entertaining audiences.

00:08:20.434 --> 00:08:22.968
But people just love "Top Gun."

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:24.734
-Yeah.
-They cannot get enough of it.

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:26.934
-I love the story, though.
I love you.

00:08:26.934 --> 00:08:28.868
You did it so -- you were --
it was just --

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:29.968
Everything was great.
-Thank you.

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:32.234
-Jennifer Connelley.
-I know, right?

00:08:32.234 --> 00:08:34.200
She's so good.
-The greatest in everything.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.734
But we had --
-Val, a nice --

00:08:35.734 --> 00:08:37.767
a really touching performance
from Val.

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.467
-I lost it.
I even knew that was

00:08:39.467 --> 00:08:41.300
gonna happen, and I --
I watched it, and I was like --

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.467
I still lost it.

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:43.634
-How did you know
it was gonna happen?

00:08:43.634 --> 00:08:45.167
-I have an inside scoop.
-A little inside --

00:08:45.167 --> 00:08:46.267
-Yeah, yeah.
-Well, you're in the biz, Jimmy.

00:08:46.267 --> 00:08:47.901
-Well, you know, I had Jon --

00:08:47.901 --> 00:08:50.801
Jon Hamm was on the show
a couple times.

00:08:50.801 --> 00:08:53.367
And he told me that, you know,
you met the royals...

00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:54.534
-Yes.
-...because you screened it

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:56.033
in London.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:58.367
-And it was like -- and it --
and he was telling me, he goes,

00:08:58.367 --> 00:09:00.467
"Yeah, it was really
interesting and fun."

00:09:00.467 --> 00:09:02.934
And he said that the cast
was all told,

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:04.868
"Hey, be very polite.
Don't say too much."

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:07.834
-Oh, they give -- they give you,
like, a full kind of rules,

00:09:07.834 --> 00:09:09.300
like do's and don'ts.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:12.567
And there's, you know, a lot of
etiquette, which deservingly so.

00:09:12.567 --> 00:09:15.868
So, yeah, I was actually --
I kind of had a sheet to prep

00:09:15.868 --> 00:09:16.934
to make sure
I didn't mess it up.

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:18.200
-But then he said --
-Yeah.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.701
-Well, I have just a photo.
And I just want you

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:21.434
to explain the photo,
'cause here's you talking.

00:09:21.434 --> 00:09:22.767
-Yeah.
-There's Jennifer Connelley.

00:09:22.767 --> 00:09:24.400
-Right.
-Little concerned.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:26.033
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:26.033 --> 00:09:27.667
-Laughing.
-Sure.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:28.834
-Right?
Kate Middleton laughing.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:29.834
And then --
-Yeah.

00:09:29.834 --> 00:09:31.501
-He's going, "Mm-hmm."
-"Mm-hmm."

00:09:31.501 --> 00:09:32.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:34.334
Yeah.
-And so what is happening?

00:09:34.334 --> 00:09:36.434
Can you tell us the story of
what's going on with this?

00:09:36.434 --> 00:09:37.934
-I think right off the bat,
I messed up.

00:09:37.934 --> 00:09:40.834
You're not supposed to, like,
extend your hand

00:09:40.834 --> 00:09:43.601
right off the bat unless --
unless they do.

00:09:43.601 --> 00:09:46.000
But I felt the vibe,
so I was like, "I'm --"

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:47.167 --> 00:09:49.467
I was like, "I'm going in.
I'm going in."

00:09:49.467 --> 00:09:51.234
-"Felt the vibe."
-And to their credit,

00:09:51.234 --> 00:09:53.501
they were very disarming,
and this and that.

00:09:53.501 --> 00:09:55.634
But, yeah, if you --
I think right there,

00:09:55.634 --> 00:09:58.667
I'm honestly lost
in Prince William's -- in his --

00:09:58.667 --> 00:10:00.501
in his eyes.
[ Laughter ]

